<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grégoire Kayibanda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1924">1924</a>–<a href="/years/1976">1976</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grégoire Kayibanda was the first President of Rwanda, from 1962 to 1973. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a> journalist and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parmehutu">Parmehutu</a> party, he co-wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu-manifesto">Hutu Manifesto</a> of 1957 and led the revolution that overthrew the Tutsi monarchy. His government favoured the Hutu majority, and repeated violence drove many Tutsi into exile. He was overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juvenal-habyarimana">Juvénal Habyarimana</a> in 1973 and died in detention.</p></div>
